# Byte-compiled / cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Environments
.venv/
venv/

# Test + coverage artefacts
.coverage
htmlcov/
.crash/

# CI definitions ARE tracked. They used to be ignored here, with a note that the
# deploy token lacked GitHub's `workflow` scope. That blocker is gone: the token
# now carries `workflows: write`, and ci.yml is committed for real. The line is
# deleted rather than left behind, because an ignore entry that quietly blocks
# the pipeline is the same shape as finding 10: a stale artefact that keeps
# explaining itself as if it were still current.
# tools\local_ci.py stays, for running the same matrix before a push.

# Atomic-write temp files (should never be committed, but if a crash left one
# behind, it is evidence, not source)
.*.tmp
.*.lock
.*.lock.stale.*

# Unpublished article drafts. Written for Habr and kept in the private companion
# repo so this repository does not pre-publish them. The ignore is here so a
# draft cannot quietly reappear in a public commit.
docs/article-*.md
